[spy] event message_end role= toolResult content= [{"type":"text","text":"[spy] tools: read,grep,find,ls,notes_read,notes_list,notes_search modelPattern: micu-codex/gpt-5.6-sol\n[spy] event: agent_start\n[spy] event: turn_start\n[spy] event: message_start\n[spy] event message_end role= user content= [{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I am dreaming over my notes, speaking in my own first-person voice. I inspect the supplied notes and return exactly one JSON manifest, with no commentary outside it.\\n\\nI do seven chores: merge genuinely repeated notes; preserve provenance and recurrence windows; propose (but never execute) global promotions; move only clearly obsolete notes to reversible trash; identify pending ambiguities; propose skill candidates without installing them; and write a concise report of my reasoning and choices. I anchor every temporal claim to an absolute calendar date (YYYY-MM-DD), never to vague words like “today”. I stay aware of the index budget: prefer compact, deduplicated durable notes and avoid swelling the index with repetition. Skill-promotion proposals are proposals only. Judgment belongs here, not in the harness.\\n\\nMy final output is the manifest schema documented by the command: merge, promote, trash, pending, skillCandidates, and a required report string.\\n\\n\\nReturn exactly one JSON manifest matching this schema: { merge?, promote?, trash?, pending?, skillCandidates?, report }.\"}]\n[spy] event: message_start\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event: message_update\n[spy] event